Dry run 2 jobs, local rehearsal of both job commands on week 5 code, 28 November 2026
Code: g10-week5-post-training at 1ee65d5c (includes lab PR #882), plus the optimizer fix of saitej123/era-v5-lab#184 and
the changes in the same pull request as this file. CPU, Python 3.11.16, torch 2.7.1+cpu. <LAB> lab checkout, <IN> private inputs, <JOB> private job folder.

What is real: the two Command lines, read from the job files with their placeholders filled in (so the comparison command
carries --dt-unseen keep); the p1536 tokenizer and KE2 byte table; 45 documents of held-out v1 (3 per slice); Team 5's
trainer, KAS V2 head, a Team 7 store.
What is a stand-in: a 2-layer, width-256 model trained 3 steps on synthetic text (run id dryrun2-1234); its delivered
manifest.json and summary.json were edited locally to smoke=false, AGREED_BASELINE_RUN and COMPLETED so that
--origin g5_delivery loads it; synthetic SFT pack shards and code tasks; --no-pack-check; small sizes appended to each
command (including --dt-calib-rows 4, so most experts get no calibration tokens here); --device cpu; the RL reward replaced
by a seeded coin (--stand-in-reward 0.4); MADE-UP benchmark rows.
Run with OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1. With torch's default threads on this laptop, two same-seed RL runs differed
from the 7th digit of the loss, and Team 7's bit-exact export probe refused a folder saved with default threads and read
with one thread. With one thread everywhere the rerun in section 4 equals the first run.
Nothing here is a quality result. Not covered: GPU and bf16, the pinned data, the dry run 2 checkpoint, Team 9's scorer.

